# Nothing here is generated by a build — this site has no build step. The two files under
# dist/ ARE tracked, deliberately, unlike the ignored dist/ folders in the app projects:
# there they are output, here they are content. The download buttons only work if the
# binaries travel with index.html, so a clone that lacks them is a broken site, and a host
# that deploys straight from this repo (GitHub Pages and friends) would serve a page whose
# downloads have quietly removed themselves.
#
# If the history ever gets too heavy for that — every published build adds another ~11MB
# blob that git keeps forever — replace this comment with `/dist/` and upload the folder
# separately. Anchor it with the leading slash: an unanchored `dist/` matches at any depth,
# which is the trap the PHP project hit when it swallowed a hand-written page.

# Windows and editor litter
Thumbs.db
desktop.ini
.DS_Store
*.swp
*~
